| 6 | 6 | 0 |\n| `verification::scope_leak_tests` | 7 | 7 | 0 |\n| `verification::incremental_tests` | 5 | 5 | 0 |\n| `verification::surfacing_tests` | 5 | 5 | 0 |\n| `verification::integration_tests` | 8 | 7 | **1** |\n\nFailing test: `verification::integration_tests::test_scope_leak_blocked_at_store_boundary_for_all_scopes` panics with `assertion failed: log_output.contains(\"scope_leak_blocked\")` at `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/integration_tests.rs:139`. Persistence assertions in the same test pass (4 SQL events recorded as expected), so store enforcement works; the tracing-substring assertion is broken because the test's thread-local `tracing::subscriber::set_default` writer doesn't observe events emitted under a pre-installed global subscriber from an earlier test in the same binary.\n\n## Issues encountered\n\nSix findings documented in the review file:\n\n1. **(Blocking)** Integration test `test_scope_leak_blocked_at_store_boundary_for_all_scopes` fails on the tracing-log substring assertion.\n2. **(Blocking)** `EventPayload::MemoryScopeFiltered` is defined in `events/kinds.rs:521-555` but never emitted to the event log — the store records only to a private SQLite table and the `tracing` stream.\n3. File-length ceiling crossed without justification — `verification/existence.rs` 803 lines, `verification/integration_tests.rs` 922 lines (ceiling 800).\n4. Function-length ceiling crossed — `verify_memory_inner` 80 lines, `on_graph_delta` 61 lines (ceiling 50).\n5. Unjustified `#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]` on `IncrementalVerifier::new` (`incremental.rs:97`).\n6. Thin coverage of two §8 verification checks (\"implementation still matches memory claim where deterministic checks are possible\"; \"contradicted/superseded states remain coherent\").\n\nFour minimum-fix tasks (R54-fix-1 through R54-fix-4) are spelled out in the review's `## Verdict` section.\n\n## Final status\n\n**Complete** — the review was produced, the task's verification commands all pass, the review's verdict is `fail` (one failing T53 integration test plus the typed-event-not-emitted spec gap), and the review enumerates the minimum-fix tasks required before R55 / Phase 8 can begin. R54 itself (the review task) is complete; Phase 7 readiness is not.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":882,"cache_read_input_tokens":183869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":882},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0696e093-0770-442b-8dc9-5393bbfcd0b6","uuid":"c6a34ba4-c1ea-4c4a-9b44-8e96c02b0bc2","request_id":"req_011Cb8CB5KHYBnYkeavhtMAB"}
