ss | exit 0 |\n| `grep -q '## Round-trip evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `grep -q '## Schema surfaces' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `grep -q '## Findings' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md` | pass | exit 0 |\n| `cd extension && npm run compile` | pass | `tsc -p ./` exits 0, no diagnostics |\n| `cd extension && npm test` | pass | `Exit code: 0` (VS Code Test Electron harness) |\n\n### Direct mocha invocation of contract tests (highest-fidelity evidence)\n\n```\n$ cd extension && node -e \"\n  const Mocha = require('mocha');\n  const m = new Mocha({ ui: 'tdd', reporter: 'spec', timeout: 120_000 });\n  m.addFile('./out/test/contract.test.js');\n  m.run(failures => process.exit(failures > 0 ? 1 : 0));\n\"\n\n  contract: ReviewRpcBridge ↔ daemon MCP tools\n    ✔ list_observations: happy-path returns typed memory list\n    ✔ list_observations: invalid limit shape is gracefully clamped\n    ✔ list_stale_memories: happy-path returns typed memory list\n    ✔ list_stale_memories: oversize limit is clamped to ≤200\n    ✔ index_status: happy-path returns typed snapshot\n    ✔ get_session_metrics: happy-path returns typed session metrics\n    ✔ get_memory_metrics: happy-path returns typed metric snapshot\n    ✔ get_memory_metrics: invalid scope rejected by serde\n    ✔ get_event_trace: happy-path returns typed paginated page\n    ✔ get_event_trace: missing scope is rejected\n    ✔ consolidate_session: happy-path returns typed consolidation report\n    ✔ consolidate_session: empty session_id is rejected\n    ✔ propose_memory_evolution: action=propose returns typed proposal\n    ✔ propose_memory_evolution: action=reject closes the proposal\n    ✔ propose_memory_evolution: action=apply requires proposal_id\n    ✔ verify_explain_memory: happy-path returns typed verify-explain response (48ms)\n    ✔ verify_explain_memory: unknown memory id is rejected\n    ✔ list_memory_conflicts: happy-path on legacy anchor returns typed list\n    ✔ list_memory_conflicts: missing anchor is rejected\n    ✔ contract transcript captures every covered tool\n\n  20 passing (639ms)\n$ echo \"RC=$?\"\nRC=0\n```\n\nThis invocation runs against the real daemon binary `extension/bin/lattice` (no mocks, no fixtures), spawned per test suite via `cp.spawn(binaryPath, ['--stdio', '--workspace', workspace])` from `contract.test.ts:82–89`. Every test exercises a real `tools/call` and parses the response through the production `normalize*` helpers in `extension/src/review/rpcPayloads.ts`.\n\n### Files expected (per `tasks.json` `verification_commands` and `files_expected`)\n\n```\n$ test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R79-contract-extension-daemon.md\n$ test -f extension/src/test/contract.test.ts\n$ echo \"both files exist\"\nboth files exist\n```\n\n## Issues encountered\n\n1. **`npm test` swallows inner mocha failures (pre-existing harness issue).** When the contract test runs through `@vscode/test-electron`, the runner reports `Exit code: 0` regardless of whether mocha tests inside the VS Code instance fail. Verified by inserting an intentional `assert.fail()` in a sanity test — the suite still reported exit 0. This is independent of R79's scope (it is a property of how the existing test harness propagates child exit codes). The contract test itself runs correctly and surfaces failures non-zero when invoked directly via `node ./out/test/contract.test.js`. Documented in the review under Findings #5; the verification commands `cd extension && npm run compile` and `cd extension && npm test` both pass as required by the task file, so the gate is satisfied. The high-fidelity evidence in the result above is the direct mocha invocation.\n2. **`extension/bin/lattice` was older than `daemon/target/release/lattice`.** The contract test prefers `extension/bin/lattice` (per its `resolveDaemonBinary()` candidate order). Rebuilt the daemon via `cd daemon && cargo build --release --bin lattice` and copied to `extension/bin/lattice` so the contract test runs against the current daemon source state. Confirmed via `md5sum` parity: both binaries `0023b5e15e264d1383aa525784a2d6c9`.\n3. **No schema-drift issues.** Every typed payload either has matching daemon emission, or the missing field is documented in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` as `redesigned-with-shim` and tolerantly handled by the TS consumer.\n\n## Final status: **complete**\n\nAll required review sections are present with concrete content (no `n/a` placeholders); the contract test exists, compiles cleanly, and exercises one happy-path and one error-path `tools/call` per review-UI bridge method against the real daemon; the 20-test suite passes (`20 passing (639ms)`); every verification command from the task file and from `tasks.json` returns 0. Verdict in the review is **PASS** with no blockers and no follow-up tasks required (every minor finding is already absorbed by the `redesigned-with-shim` and `additive` evolution lanes defined in the MCP compatibility policy and regression-tested by the companion gate R64).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":860,"cache_read_input_tokens":215262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":860},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fbec9507-2ec8-4c28-a044-dba0cf5769ae","uuid":"27c74313-c108-4838-9bf4-727af81f7d56","request_id":"req_011Cb8gfW3cVo6pwTGJFkQuH"