docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T71.log:1980:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/R64.log:19:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q8zXx9EGAweYDDHMeCugFu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# MCP Tool Reference\n2\t\n3\tThis document is the canonical Phase 8 MCP tool listing for the cognitive workspace fork. It implements the contract requested by [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface), [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles), and [## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2). Collapse decisions and shim rationale are recorded in [MCP Surface Audit](./2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md). Compatibility and removal rules come from [MCP Compatibility Policy](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md).\n4\t\n5\tImplementation source of truth: advertised tools are assembled in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs::handle_tools_list`; callable names are dispatched in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs::handle_tools_call`.\n6\t\n7\t## Final tool list\n8\t\n9\tLegend: `generic events` means the daemon records `ToolCalled` and `ToolResult` when event capture is enabled. `workflow events` means the workflow response also carries the Phase 8 standard sequence `AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, and `PlanCreated` in its workflow event metadata.\n10\t\n11\t| Tool | Description | Request schema summary | Response schema summary | Render modes and handles | Budget controls | Phase 2 events | Deprecation status | Implementing file |\n12\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n13\t| `get_context_capsule` | First discovery tool for unfamiliar code areas; returns ranked source pivots, nearby symbols, reusable handle, and suggested expansion. | `query` required; optional `mode`, `render`. | Overview, pivots, context, memory highlights, stats, `context_handle`, `suggested_expand`, structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=full/focused`; emits context handle and expansion target. | Focused mode bounds pivots/context; render options shape payload. | generic events; workflow response metadata. | Stable canonical; `query_context` callable alias. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/context_capsule.rs` |\n14\t| `prepare_change` | First workflow tool for fix/add/refactor work once the area is known; returns likely edit files, symbols, tests, risks, and memory. | `query` required; optional `entry_files`, `entry_symbols`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Workflow bundle with ranked pivots, context, tests, risks, memory, events, handle, and structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget=tiny/compact/full`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/prepare_change.rs` |\n15\t| `plan_edit` | Patch-oriented planning bundle for likely edit files, candidate spans, affected callers/dependencies, docs, and recommended tests. | `query` required; optional `entry_files`, `entry_symbols`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Edit-planning workflow bundle with spans, impacted symbols, docs, tests, risks, memory, events, and handle. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/plan_edit.rs` |\n16\t| `trace_scenario` | Scenario-debugging bundle that traces likely execution paths, guards, side effects, and failure branches. | `scenario` required; optional `entry_files`, `entry_symbols`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Scenario workflow bundle with paths, branches, guards, risks, context, memory, events, and handle. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/trace_scenario.rs` |\n17\t| `find_relevant_tests` | Finds tests most relevant to files, symbols, or a diff. | Optional `files`, `symbols`, `diff`, `limit`. | Ranked test list with reasons and structured payload. | Structured response; context handle is stored for expansion. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events; workflow metadata for v2 bundle. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/relevant_tests.rs` |\n18\t| `impact_from_diff` | Reviews a local diff for changed symbols, downstream impact, risks, checklist, and tests. | `diff` required; optional `files`, `symbols`, `hops`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Impact workflow bundle with changed symbols, dependent paths, risks, tests, docs, memory, events, and handle. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `hops`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow metadata. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/impact_from_diff.rs` |\n19\t| `get_working_set_context` | Compresses already-known files/symbols into a bundle of nearby code, docs, tests, and memory. | Optional `files`, `symbols`, `query`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Working-set workflow bundle with pivots, context, tests, docs, memory, risks, handle, and structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n20\t| `summarize_subsystem` | Summary-first map for an unfamiliar subsystem with key files, symbols, tests, and durable memory. | `query` required; optional `files`, `symbols`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Subsystem summary bundle with files, symbols, tests, memory, risks, handle, and structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n21\t| `get_repo_playbook` | Repo-wide startup summary of architecture, conventions, high-signal files, and durable patterns. | Optional `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Playbook bundle with architecture summary, conventions, files, memory, and structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n22\t| `get_docs_capsule` | Finds relevant Markdown docs and sections for a question, plus code symbols mentioned from those docs. | `query` required; optional `files`, `symbols`, `limit`. | Ranked docs/sections, related symbols, reasons, and expansion handle. | Structured response with stable doc/section expansion targets. | `limit` bounds docs. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/docs_capsule.rs` |\n23\t| `get_backlinks` | Returns inbound Markdown references to a symbol, file, document, or section. | `target` required; optional `kind`, `limit`. | Inbound reference list with target metadata and reasons. | Structured response with file/doc/section targets. | `limit` bounds references. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n24\t| `get_outgoing_links` | Returns outgoing Markdown links and code mentions from a document, section, symbol, or file. | `target` required; optional `kind`, `limit`. | Outgoing reference list with target metadata and reasons. | Structured response with file/doc/section targets. | `limit` bounds references. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n25\t| `find_stale_docs` | Finds Markdown docs or sections likely stale against changed files or symbols. | Optional `files`, `symbols`, `limit`. | Stale-doc candidates with reasons and related symbols/files. | Structured response with doc/section targets. | `limit` bounds candidates. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n26\t| `diagnose_failure` | First failure tool for compiler errors, failing tests, and stack traces. | `input` required; optional `kind`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Failure workflow bundle with suspects, related code, tests, next steps, diagnostics, and handle. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/diagnose_failure.rs` |\n27\t| `record_workflow_outcome` | Distills successful or failed coding outcomes into durable memory. | `task` required; optional `status`, `summary`, `context_handle`, `files`, `symbols`, `tests`. | Stored outcome memory/provenance response. | Structured response; context handle may seed linked evidence. | No explicit budget. | generic events; may create memory. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n28\t| `expand_context` | Expands one suggested file, symbol, test, memory, or handle target from a prior workflow. | `handle` and `focus` required; optional `max_tokens`. | Focused expansion payload with source/context details. | Uses stable context handles and expansion targets. | `max_tokens` hard cap. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n29\t| `get_symbol` | Returns detailed information about a specific symbol by name and file. | `name`, `file` required; optional `detail`. | Symbol summary or full source/dependency metadata. | `detail=summary/full`; stable symbol identity where available. | Detail mode bounds payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n30\t| `get_dependents` | Returns symbols that depend on the given symbol. | `name`, `file` required. | Incoming dependency list. | Structured graph response. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n31\t| `get_dependencies` | Returns symbols the given symbol depends on. | `name`, `file` required. | Outgoing dependency list. | Structured graph response. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n32\t| `get_impact_graph` | Computes transitive dependents for a symbol up to N hops. | `name`, `file` required; optional `hops`. | Impact graph nodes/edges. | Structured graph response. | `hops` bounds traversal. | generic events. | Stable canonical; `blast_radius` callable alias. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n33\t| `search_symbols` | Searches symbols by case-insensitive name pattern. | `pattern` required; optional `limit`, `detail`. | Ranked symbol matches. | `detail=summary/full`. | `limit` bounds matches. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n34\t| `get_skeleton` | Token-efficient file structure view with symbols, kinds, and dependent counts. | `file` required. | File skeleton and symbol metadata. | Structured file expansion target. | Skeleton shape bounds payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical; `get_file_context` callable alias. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n35\t| `save_observation` | Legacy observation-centric memory write for observation, decision, exploration, pattern, or anti-pattern. | `content` required; optional `memory_type`, links, `scope`, `workspace_id`, `branch`, `refresh_key`. | Stored memory id and metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory write path. | Redesigned-with-shim; successor direction is `save_memory`. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n36\t| `get_session_context` | Legacy session-context recall across current and previous sessions. | Optional `query`, `limit`. | Session memory list. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds memories. | generic events. | Redesigned-with-shim; successor direction is `get_task_memory`. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n37\t| `search_memory` | Required workflow tool for searching stored memories by query. | `query` required; optional `limit`. | Ranked memory matches. | Structured response with memory metadata. | `limit` bounds matches. | generic events. | Stable canonical; `recall_memories` callable alias. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n38\t| `search_logic_flow` | Finds execution paths between functions. | `from`, `to` required; optional `from_file`, `to_file`, `max_depth`. | Call chains between source and target symbols. | Structured graph response. | `max_depth` bounds traversal. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n39\t| `submit_lsp_edges` | Adds high-confidence LSP call-hierarchy edges to the graph. | `edges[]` required with from/to names/files and optional kind. | Edge insertion summary. | Structured response. | Input array bounds work. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n40\t| `workspace_setup` | Returns workspace conventions, language breakdown, and recommended configuration. | Optional `format`. | Markdown or JSON setup summary. | `format=json/markdown`. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n41\t| `index_status` | Reports current indexing status, graph stats, and language breakdown. | No arguments. | Operational status snapshot. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n42\t| `get_session_metrics` | Reports live assistant-session workflow metrics. | No arguments. | Metrics such as tool calls, payload sizes, handle reuse, and automatic memory writes. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | Not self-counted; other calls record generic metrics. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n43\t| `get_project_rules` | Returns project-specific rules and conventions. | No arguments. | Rule summary. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n44\t| `inspect_working_memory` | Inspects current working-memory state for a task with compact summary or diagnostic snapshot. | `task_id` required; optional `mode`, `include_excluded`. | Compact summary or diagnostic state plus checkpoint id and expansion handle. | `mode=compact/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Mode bounds payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs` |\n45\t| `list_observations` | Lists stored observations and memories, newest first. | Optional `session_id`, `limit`. | Memory list excluding invalidated records. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n46\t| `list_stale_memories` | Lists stale memories likely needing review or refresh. | Optional `query`, `limit`. | Stale memory candidates. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n47\t| `promote_observation` | Promotes session memory into branch or repo scope with metadata. | `id`, `scope` required; optional links, workspace, branch, `refresh_key`. | Promotion result and updated metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory write path. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n48\t| `refresh_memory` | Refreshes memory evidence and metadata while preserving identity and clearing stale state. | `id` required; optional content, type, scope, links, workspace, branch, freshness, confidence. | Updated memory metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory update path. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n49\t| `delete_observation` | Deletes a stored observation by id. | `id` required. | Delete confirmation. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory lifecycle path. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n50\t| `update_observation` | Updates observation content in place and clears stale flags. | `id`, `content` required. | Updated memory metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory update path. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n51\t| `consolidate_session` | Triggers proposal-only session consolidation and returns auditable proposal ids. | `session_id` required; optional `mode`, `budget_ms`, `render_mode`. | Consolidation report with proposals, categories, incomplete flag, and notes. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | `budget_ms`; render mode bounds detail. | generic events; `MemoryConsolidated`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs` |\n52\t| `get_memory_metrics` | Returns Phase 9 memory and workflow metrics with provenance and honest nulls for unavailable signals. | Optional `scope`, `time_range`, `signals`, `render_mode`. | Metric snapshot with requested signals, values, provenance, and availability. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | Requested `signals` and render mode bound payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs` |\n53\t| `get_event_trace` | Returns paginated, workspace-bounded event traces for task, session, or workspace scopes. | Optional `task_id`, `session_id`, `workspace_id`, `kinds`, `since`, `until`, `cursor`, `limit`, `render_mode`. | Event page with scope, events, cursor, payloads in full/diagnostic, hashes in diagnostic. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; event expansion handles. | `limit`, cursor pagination, filters, render mode. | generic events; returns event records. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs` |\n54\t| `get_task_memory` | Reads working memory plus relevant durable memory for the current task. | `task_id` required; optional `intent_hint`, `budget_tokens`. | Task memory bundle with inclusion reasons, verification/freshness/conflict state, and expansion handles. | Full structured bundle with memory expansion handles. | `budget_tokens` clips memory payload. | generic events; `MemoryRetrieved`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_task_memory.rs` |\n55\t| `save_memory` | Creates a durable memory with evidence, validity conditions, invalidation triggers, and queued verification. | Memory content/type/scope/evidence/link fields; validation requires a meaningful claim and scope. | Created memory response with metadata, verification state, and expansion handle. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; `MemoryCreated`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/save_memory.rs` |\n56\t| `propose_memory_evolution` | Persists, applies, or rejects auditable memory-evolution proposals. | `action` required; proposal actions accept `proposal_id`, `memory_id`, content, links, validity, invalidation, supersession, reason, and actor fields as applicable. | Evolution proposal/result with proposal id, action, proposed memory state, decision metadata, and optional deprecation warning for shimmed calls. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; apply/reject emits consolidation/update lifecycle through memory path. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |\n57\t| `apply_memory_evolution` | Deprecated advertised shim for applying an existing evolution proposal. | `proposal_id` required; optional `reason`, `decided_by`. | Same result as `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"apply\")` plus `deprecation_warning`. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; canonical action path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |\n58\t| `verify_explain_memory` | Runs fresh verification checks for a durable memory or explains the last persisted report. | `memory_id` required; optional `mode`, `render_mode`. | Verification status, checks, confidence delta, expansion handle, summary lines, optional diagnostic trace. | `mode=verify/explain/verify_and_explain`; `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; verification memory retrieval/invalidation as applicable. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |\n59\t| `verify_memory` | Deprecated advertised shim for verification-only mode. | Same as `verify_explain_memory`; shim forces `mode=verify`. | Same response as canonical verify mode plus `deprecation_warning`. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; canonical mode path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |\n60\t| `explain_memory` | Deprecated advertised shim for explanation-only mode. | Same as `verify_explain_memory`; shim forces `mode=explain`. | Same response as canonical explain mode plus `deprecation_warning`. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; canonical mode path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |\n61\t| `list_memory_conflicts` | Lists contradiction and supersession edges anchored on a memory or graph node. | Anchor identity or legacy memory id; optional scope, pagination, and `render_mode`. | Conflict page with anchors, edges, summaries, and pagination. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | Pagination and render mode bound payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/list_memory_conflicts.rs` |\n62\t\n63\t### Callable deprecated aliases\n64\t\n65\tThese names are accepted by `handle_tools_call` but are not advertised in `tools/list`. They remain compatibility debt governed by [## Legacy aliases and deadlines](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#legacy-aliases-and-deadlines) and [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol).\n66\t\n67\t| Alias | Canonical target | Request and response compatibility | Events | Implementing file |\n68\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n69\t| `query_context` | `get_context_capsule` | Accepts the legacy context-query request and returns the canonical context capsule shape. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n70\t| `blast_radius` | `get_impact_graph` | Accepts the legacy impact request and returns impact graph output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n71\t| `get_file_context` | `get_skeleton` | Accepts the legacy file-context request and returns skeleton output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n72\t| `store_memory` | `save_observation` | Accepts the legacy memory-store request and returns observation memory output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n73\t| `recall_memories` | `search_memory` | Accepts the legacy recall request and returns memory search output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n74\t\n75\t## Render modes\n76\t\n77\t[## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) requires compact rendering, full structured JSON, context handles, stable expansion targets, budget controls, and diagnostic explanations where useful. [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles) requires compact/full render choice and structured payloads.\n78\t\n79\tWorkflow tools use `render=json|markdown|hybrid` for delivery shape and `mode=auto|compact|full` when a workflow bundle supports response density. `get_context_capsule` keeps its older `mode=full|focused` discovery control. Memory v2 administrative tools use `render_mode=compact|full|diagnostic`; `verify_explain_memory` additionally uses `mode=verify|explain|verify_and_explain`.\n80\t\n81\tDiagnostic render modes are reserved for traceability: they may include check traces, ranking reasons, payload hashes, spilled-payload row ids, or excluded candidates. Compact modes must remain bounded enough for repeated assistant use.\n82\t\n83\t## Expansion handles\n84\t\n85\tWorkflow responses that return bundles store context handles through `context_cache` and expose `suggested_expand` targets. `expand_context` is the canonical follow-up tool and accepts a prior `handle` plus a `focus` such as a file, symbol, test, memory, or stable identity. Memory-bearing responses expose memory or event expansion handles where useful: `get_task_memory`, `verify_explain_memory`, `get_event_trace`, and `inspect_working_memory` all return handles for focused follow-up.\n86\t\n87\tHandles must stay workspace-bound and must not bypass the path scoping, ignored-directory rules, or memory scoping required by the repo contract. Expired, missing, or invalid handles should fail with actionable errors rather than silently returning unrelated context.\n88\t\n89\t## Budget controls\n90\t\n91\tBudget controls are part of the MCP contract in [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface). Workflow bundle tools accept `budget=tiny|compact|full`, `max_tokens`, and `wire_format=standard|dense` where listed. The daemon constants are `tiny=260`, `compact=850`, and `full=2600` approximate workflow token caps unless a stricter `max_tokens` is supplied.\n92\t\n93\tOther tools expose narrower controls: `limit` bounds list/search/event outputs, `hops` and `max_depth` bound graph traversal, `budget_tokens` bounds `get_task_memory`, `budget_ms` bounds synchronous consolidation, cursor pagination bounds `get_event_trace`, and render modes bound diagnostic detail.\n94\t\n95\t## Deprecation policy\n96\t\n97\tDeprecation follows [## Backward compatibility](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#backward-compatibility) and [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). A redesigned tool must keep maintained clients working for one full numbered phase cycle. The legacy request shape must remain accepted, responses must remain parseable, and new identity/event/ranking/memory fields must be additive unless a shim explicitly documents a successor contract.\n98\t\n99\tThe Phase 8 advertised deprecated shims are `apply_memory_evolution`, `verify_memory`, and `explain_memory`. The callable-only legacy aliases are `query_context`, `blast_radius`, `get_file_context`, `store_memory`, and `recall_memories`. Removal requires a phase boundary, migrated first-party docs/fixtures/prompts/cached examples, compatibility tests, and an architecture-doc update in the same change.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1872dd72-ab0d-4621-9b2e-b0d7d6173b92","uuid":"beaa81a9-9233-4fba-b08e-9b72255ac693","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:51:26.026Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md","content":"# MCP Tool Reference\n\nThis document is the canonical Phase 8 MCP tool listing for the cognitive workspace fork. It implements the contract requested by [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface), [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles), and [## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-8-workflow-engine-v2). Collapse decisions and shim rationale are recorded in [MCP Surface Audit](./2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md). Compatibility and removal rules come from [MCP Compatibility Policy](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md).\n\nImplementation source of truth: advertised tools are assembled in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs::handle_tools_list`; callable names are dispatched in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs::handle_tools_call`.\n\n## Final tool list\n\nLegend: `generic events` means the daemon records `ToolCalled` and `ToolResult` when event capture is enabled. `workflow events` means the workflow response also carries the Phase 8 standard sequence `AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, and `PlanCreated` in its workflow event metadata.\n\n| Tool | Description | Request schema summary | Response schema summary | Render modes and handles | Budget controls | Phase 2 events | Deprecation status | Implementing file |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `get_context_capsule` | First discovery tool for unfamiliar code areas; returns ranked source pivots, nearby symbols, reusable handle, and suggested expansion. | `query` required; optional `mode`, `render`. | Overview, pivots, context, memory highlights, stats, `context_handle`, `suggested_expand`, structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=full/focused`; emits context handle and expansion target. | Focused mode bounds pivots/context; render options shape payload. | generic events; workflow response metadata. | Stable canonical; `query_context` callable alias. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/context_capsule.rs` |\n| `prepare_change` | First workflow tool for fix/add/refactor work once the area is known; returns likely edit files, symbols, tests, risks, and memory. | `query` required; optional `entry_files`, `entry_symbols`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Workflow bundle with ranked pivots, context, tests, risks, memory, events, handle, and structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget=tiny/compact/full`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/prepare_change.rs` |\n| `plan_edit` | Patch-oriented planning bundle for likely edit files, candidate spans, affected callers/dependencies, docs, and recommended tests. | `query` required; optional `entry_files`, `entry_symbols`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Edit-planning workflow bundle with spans, impacted symbols, docs, tests, risks, memory, events, and handle. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/plan_edit.rs` |\n| `trace_scenario` | Scenario-debugging bundle that traces likely execution paths, guards, side effects, and failure branches. | `scenario` required; optional `entry_files`, `entry_symbols`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Scenario workflow bundle with paths, branches, guards, risks, context, memory, events, and handle. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/trace_scenario.rs` |\n| `find_relevant_tests` | Finds tests most relevant to files, symbols, or a diff. | Optional `files`, `symbols`, `diff`, `limit`. | Ranked test list with reasons and structured payload. | Structured response; context handle is stored for expansion. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events; workflow metadata for v2 bundle. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/relevant_tests.rs` |\n| `impact_from_diff` | Reviews a local diff for changed symbols, downstream impact, risks, checklist, and tests. | `diff` required; optional `files`, `symbols`, `hops`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Impact workflow bundle with changed symbols, dependent paths, risks, tests, docs, memory, events, and handle. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `hops`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow metadata. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/impact_from_diff.rs` |\n| `get_working_set_context` | Compresses already-known files/symbols into a bundle of nearby code, docs, tests, and memory. | Optional `files`, `symbols`, `query`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Working-set workflow bundle with pivots, context, tests, docs, memory, risks, handle, and structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `summarize_subsystem` | Summary-first map for an unfamiliar subsystem with key files, symbols, tests, and durable memory. | `query` required; optional `files`, `symbols`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Subsystem summary bundle with files, symbols, tests, memory, risks, handle, and structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_repo_playbook` | Repo-wide startup summary of architecture, conventions, high-signal files, and durable patterns. | Optional `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Playbook bundle with architecture summary, conventions, files, memory, and structured payload. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_docs_capsule` | Finds relevant Markdown docs and sections for a question, plus code symbols mentioned from those docs. | `query` required; optional `files`, `symbols`, `limit`. | Ranked docs/sections, related symbols, reasons, and expansion handle. | Structured response with stable doc/section expansion targets. | `limit` bounds docs. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/docs_capsule.rs` |\n| `get_backlinks` | Returns inbound Markdown references to a symbol, file, document, or section. | `target` required; optional `kind`, `limit`. | Inbound reference list with target metadata and reasons. | Structured response with file/doc/section targets. | `limit` bounds references. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_outgoing_links` | Returns outgoing Markdown links and code mentions from a document, section, symbol, or file. | `target` required; optional `kind`, `limit`. | Outgoing reference list with target metadata and reasons. | Structured response with file/doc/section targets. | `limit` bounds references. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `find_stale_docs` | Finds Markdown docs or sections likely stale against changed files or symbols. | Optional `files`, `symbols`, `limit`. | Stale-doc candidates with reasons and related symbols/files. | Structured response with doc/section targets. | `limit` bounds candidates. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `diagnose_failure` | First failure tool for compiler errors, failing tests, and stack traces. | `input` required; optional `kind`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Failure workflow bundle with suspects, related code, tests, next steps, diagnostics, and handle. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/diagnose_failure.rs` |\n| `record_workflow_outcome` | Distills successful or failed coding outcomes into durable memory. | `task` required; optional `status`, `summary`, `context_handle`, `files`, `symbols`, `tests`. | Stored outcome memory/provenance response. | Structured response; context handle may seed linked evidence. | No explicit budget. | generic events; may create memory. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `expand_context` | Expands one suggested file, symbol, test, memory, or handle target from a prior workflow. | `handle` and `focus` required; optional `max_tokens`. | Focused expansion payload with source/context details. | Uses stable context handles and expansion targets. | `max_tokens` hard cap. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_symbol` | Returns detailed information about a specific symbol by name and file. | `name`, `file` required; optional `detail`. | Symbol summary or full source/dependency metadata. | `detail=summary/full`; stable symbol identity where available. | Detail mode bounds payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_dependents` | Returns symbols that depend on the given symbol. | `name`, `file` required. | Incoming dependency list. | Structured graph response. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_dependencies` | Returns symbols the given symbol depends on. | `name`, `file` required. | Outgoing dependency list. | Structured graph response. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_impact_graph` | Computes transitive dependents for a symbol up to N hops. | `name`, `file` required; optional `hops`. | Impact graph nodes/edges. | Structured graph response. | `hops` bounds traversal. | generic events. | Stable canonical; `blast_radius` callable alias. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `search_symbols` | Searches symbols by case-insensitive name pattern. | `pattern` required; optional `limit`, `detail`. | Ranked symbol matches. | `detail=summary/full`. | `limit` bounds matches. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_skeleton` | Token-efficient file structure view with symbols, kinds, and dependent counts. | `file` required. | File skeleton and symbol metadata. | Structured file expansion target. | Skeleton shape bounds payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical; `get_file_context` callable alias. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `save_observation` | Legacy observation-centric memory write for observation, decision, exploration, pattern, or anti-pattern. | `content` required; optional `memory_type`, links, `scope`, `workspace_id`, `branch`, `refresh_key`. | Stored memory id and metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory write path. | Redesigned-with-shim; successor direction is `save_memory`. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_session_context` | Legacy session-context recall across current and previous sessions. | Optional `query`, `limit`. | Session memory list. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds memories. | generic events. | Redesigned-with-shim; successor direction is `get_task_memory`. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `search_memory` | Required workflow tool for searching stored memories by query. | `query` required; optional `limit`. | Ranked memory matches. | Structured response with memory metadata. | `limit` bounds matches. | generic events. | Stable canonical; `recall_memories` callable alias. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `search_logic_flow` | Finds execution paths between functions. | `from`, `to` required; optional `from_file`, `to_file`, `max_depth`. | Call chains between source and target symbols. | Structured graph response. | `max_depth` bounds traversal. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `submit_lsp_edges` | Adds high-confidence LSP call-hierarchy edges to the graph. | `edges[]` required with from/to names/files and optional kind. | Edge insertion summary. | Structured response. | Input array bounds work. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `workspace_setup` | Returns workspace conventions, language breakdown, and recommended configuration. | Optional `format`. | Markdown or JSON setup summary. | `format=json/markdown`. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `index_status` | Reports current indexing status, graph stats, and language breakdown. | No arguments. | Operational status snapshot. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_session_metrics` | Reports live assistant-session workflow metrics. | No arguments. | Metrics such as tool calls, payload sizes, handle reuse, and automatic memory writes. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | Not self-counted; other calls record generic metrics. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_project_rules` | Returns project-specific rules and conventions. | No arguments. | Rule summary. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `inspect_working_memory` | Inspects current working-memory state for a task with compact summary or diagnostic snapshot. | `task_id` required; optional `mode`, `include_excluded`. | Compact summary or diagnostic state plus checkpoint id and expansion handle. | `mode=compact/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Mode bounds payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs` |\n| `list_observations` | Lists stored observations and memories, newest first. | Optional `session_id`, `limit`. | Memory list excluding invalidated records. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `list_stale_memories` | Lists stale memories likely needing review or refresh. | Optional `query`, `limit`. | Stale memory candidates. | Structured response. | `limit` bounds results. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `promote_observation` | Promotes session memory into branch or repo scope with metadata. | `id`, `scope` required; optional links, workspace, branch, `refresh_key`. | Promotion result and updated metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory write path. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `refresh_memory` | Refreshes memory evidence and metadata while preserving identity and clearing stale state. | `id` required; optional content, type, scope, links, workspace, branch, freshness, confidence. | Updated memory metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory update path. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `delete_observation` | Deletes a stored observation by id. | `id` required. | Delete confirmation. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory lifecycle path. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `update_observation` | Updates observation content in place and clears stale flags. | `id`, `content` required. | Updated memory metadata. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; memory update path. | Redesigned-with-shim. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `consolidate_session` | Triggers proposal-only session consolidation and returns auditable proposal ids. | `session_id` required; optional `mode`, `budget_ms`, `render_mode`. | Consolidation report with proposals, categories, incomplete flag, and notes. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | `budget_ms`; render mode bounds detail. | generic events; `MemoryConsolidated`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs` |\n| `get_memory_metrics` | Returns Phase 9 memory and workflow metrics with provenance and honest nulls for unavailable signals. | Optional `scope`, `time_range`, `signals`, `render_mode`. | Metric snapshot with requested signals, values, provenance, and availability. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | Requested `signals` and render mode bound payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs` |\n| `get_event_trace` | Returns paginated, workspace-bounded event traces for task, session, or workspace scopes. | Optional `task_id`, `session_id`, `workspace_id`, `kinds`, `since`, `until`, `cursor`, `limit`, `render_mode`. | Event page with scope, events, cursor, payloads in full/diagnostic, hashes in diagnostic. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; event expansion handles. | `limit`, cursor pagination, filters, render mode. | generic events; returns event records. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs` |\n| `get_task_memory` | Reads working memory plus relevant durable memory for the current task. | `task_id` required; optional `intent_hint`, `budget_tokens`. | Task memory bundle with inclusion reasons, verification/freshness/conflict state, and expansion handles. | Full structured bundle with memory expansion handles. | `budget_tokens` clips memory payload. | generic events; `MemoryRetrieved`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_task_memory.rs` |\n| `save_memory` | Creates a durable memory with evidence, validity conditions, invalidation triggers, and queued verification. | Memory content/type/scope/evidence/link fields; validation requires a meaningful claim and scope. | Created memory response with metadata, verification state, and expansion handle. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; `MemoryCreated`. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/save_memory.rs` |\n| `propose_memory_evolution` | Persists, applies, or rejects auditable memory-evolution proposals. | `action` required; proposal actions accept `proposal_id`, `memory_id`, content, links, validity, invalidation, supersession, reason, and actor fields as applicable. | Evolution proposal/result with proposal id, action, proposed memory state, decision metadata, and optional deprecation warning for shimmed calls. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; apply/reject emits consolidation/update lifecycle through memory path. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |\n| `apply_memory_evolution` | Deprecated advertised shim for applying an existing evolution proposal. | `proposal_id` required; optional `reason`, `decided_by`. | Same result as `propose_memory_evolution(action=\"apply\")` plus `deprecation_warning`. | Structured response. | No explicit budget. | generic events; canonical action path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` |\n| `verify_explain_memory` | Runs fresh verification checks for a durable memory or explains the last persisted report. | `memory_id` required; optional `mode`, `render_mode`. | Verification status, checks, confidence delta, expansion handle, summary lines, optional diagnostic trace. | `mode=verify/explain/verify_and_explain`; `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; verification memory retrieval/invalidation as applicable. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |\n| `verify_memory` | Deprecated advertised shim for verification-only mode. | Same as `verify_explain_memory`; shim forces `mode=verify`. | Same response as canonical verify mode plus `deprecation_warning`. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; canonical mode path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |\n| `explain_memory` | Deprecated advertised shim for explanation-only mode. | Same as `verify_explain_memory`; shim forces `mode=explain`. | Same response as canonical explain mode plus `deprecation_warning`. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; canonical mode path. | Deprecated shim; remove per compatibility policy. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |\n| `list_memory_conflicts` | Lists contradiction and supersession edges anchored on a memory or graph node. | Anchor identity or legacy memory id; optional scope, pagination, and `render_mode`. | Conflict page with anchors, edges, summaries, and pagination. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`. | Pagination and render mode bound payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/list_memory_conflicts.rs` |\n\n### Callable deprecated aliases\n\nThese names are accepted by `handle_tools_call` but are not advertised in `tools/list`. They remain compatibility debt governed by [## Legacy aliases and deadlines](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#legacy-aliases-and-deadlines) and [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol).\n\n| Alias | Canonical target | Request and response compatibility | Events | Implementing file |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `query_context` | `get_context_capsule` | Accepts the legacy context-query request and returns the canonical context capsule shape. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `blast_radius` | `get_impact_graph` | Accepts the legacy impact request and returns impact graph output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `get_file_context` | `get_skeleton` | Accepts the legacy file-context request and returns skeleton output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `store_memory` | `save_observation` | Accepts the legacy memory-store request and returns observation memory output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n| `recall_memories` | `search_memory` | Accepts the legacy recall request and returns memory search output. | generic events under alias name. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` |\n\n## Render modes\n\n[## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface) requires compact rendering, full structured JSON, context handles, stable expansion targets, budget controls, and diagnostic explanations where useful. [## MCP Tool Contract Principles](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles) requires compact/full render choice and structured payloads.\n\nWorkflow tools use `render=json|markdown|hybrid` for delivery shape and `mode=auto|compact|full` when a workflow bundle supports response density. `get_context_capsule` keeps its older `mode=full|focused` discovery control. Memory v2 administrative tools use `render_mode=compact|full|diagnostic`; `verify_explain_memory` additionally uses `mode=verify|explain|verify_and_explain`.\n\nDiagnostic render modes are reserved for traceability: they may include check traces, ranking reasons, payload hashes, spilled-payload row ids, or excluded candidates. Compact modes must remain bounded enough for repeated assistant use.\n\n## Expansion handles\n\nWorkflow responses that return bundles store context handles through `context_cache` and expose `suggested_expand` targets. `expand_context` is the canonical follow-up tool and accepts a prior `handle` plus a `focus` such as a file, symbol, test, memory, or stable identity. Memory-bearing responses expose memory or event expansion handles where useful: `get_task_memory`, `verify_explain_memory`, `get_event_trace`, and `inspect_working_memory` all return handles for focused follow-up.\n\nHandles must stay workspace-bound and must not bypass the path scoping, ignored-directory rules, or memory scoping required by the repo contract. Expired, missing, or invalid handles should fail with actionable errors rather than silently returning unrelated context.\n\n## Budget controls\n\nBudget controls are part of the MCP contract in [## MCP Surface](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-surface). Workflow bundle tools accept `budget=tiny|compact|full`, `max_tokens`, and `wire_format=standard|dense` where listed. The daemon constants are `tiny=260`, `compact=850`, and `full=2600` approximate workflow token caps unless a stricter `max_tokens` is supplied.\n\nOther tools expose narrower controls: `limit` bounds list/search/event outputs, `hops` and `max_depth` bound graph traversal, `budget_tokens` bounds `get_task_memory`, `budget_ms` bounds synchronous consolidation, cursor pagination bounds `get_event_trace`, and render modes bound diagnostic detail.\n\n## Deprecation policy\n\nDeprecation follows [## Backward compatibility](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#backward-compatibility) and [## Shim removal protocol](./2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md#shim-removal-protocol). A redesigned tool must keep maintained clients working for one full numbered phase cycle. The legacy request shape must remain accepted, responses must remain parseable, and new identity/event/ranking/memory fields must be additive unless a shim explicitly documents a successor contract.\n\nThe Phase 8 advertised deprecated shims are `apply_memory_evolution`, `verify_memory`, and `explain_memory`. The callable-only legacy aliases are `query_context`, `blast_radius`, `get_file_context`, `store_memory`, and `recall_memories`. Removal requires a phase boundary, migrated first-party docs/fixtures/prompts/cached examples, compatibility tests, and an architecture-doc update in the same change.\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":100}}}
